#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM percuma tentang maklumat dan pengiraan kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Superdense coding"
msgstr "Pengekodan suprapadat"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore mapsto */}\n"
"Superdense coding is a protocol that, in some sense, achieves a complementary aim to teleportation.\n"
"Rather than allowing for the transmission of one qubit using two classical bits of communication (at the cost of one e-bit of entanglement), it allows for the transmission of two classical bits using one qubit of quantum communication (again, at the cost of one e-bit of entanglement).\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore mapsto */}\n"
"Pengekodan suprapadat ialah protokol yang, dalam erti kata tertentu, mencapai matlamat yang pelengkap kepada teleportasi.\n"
"Daripada membolehkan penghantaran satu qubit menggunakan dua bit komunikasi klasik (pada kos satu e-bit belitan), ia membolehkan penghantaran dua bit klasik menggunakan satu qubit komunikasi kuantum (sekali lagi, pada kos satu e-bit belitan).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In greater detail, we have a sender (Alice) and a receiver (Bob) that share one e-bit of entanglement.\n"
"According to the conventions in place for the lesson, this means that Alice holds a qubit $\\mathsf{A}$, Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B}$, and together the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is in the state $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$.\n"
"Alice wishes to transmit two classical bits to Bob, which we'll denote by $c$ and $d$, and she will accomplish this by sending him one qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara lebih terperinci, kita mempunyai penghantar (Alice) dan penerima (Bob) yang berkongsi satu e-bit belitan.\n"
"Mengikut konvensyen yang ditetapkan untuk pelajaran ini, ini bermakna Alice memegang qubit $\\mathsf{A}$, Bob memegang qubit $\\mathsf{B}$, dan bersama-sama pasangan $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ berada dalam keadaan $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$.\n"
"Alice ingin menghantar dua bit klasik kepada Bob, yang akan kita tandakan sebagai $c$ dan $d$, dan dia akan melakukan ini dengan menghantar satu qubit kepadanya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is reasonable to view this feat as being less interesting than the one that teleportation accomplishes.\n"
"Sending qubits is likely to be so much more difficult than sending classical bits for the foreseeable future that trading one qubit of quantum communication for two bits of classical communication, at the cost of an e-bit no less, hardly seems worth it.\n"
"However, this does not imply that superdense coding is not interesting, for it most certainly is.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada baiknya untuk melihat pencapaian ini sebagai kurang menarik daripada yang dicapai oleh teleportasi.\n"
"Menghantar qubit berkemungkinan besar jauh lebih sukar daripada menghantar bit klasik untuk masa yang boleh diramalkan sehingga pertukaran satu qubit komunikasi kuantum dengan dua bit komunikasi klasik, pada kos e-bit pula, hampir tidak berbaloi.\n"
"Walau bagaimanapun, ini tidak bermakna pengekodan suprapadat tidak menarik, kerana ia memang menarik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fitting the theme of the lesson, one reason why superdense coding is interesting is that it demonstrates a concrete and (in the context of information theory) rather striking use of entanglement.\n"
"A famous theorem in quantum information theory, known as *Holevo's theorem*, implies that without the use of a shared entangled state, it is impossible to communicate more than one bit of classical information by sending a single qubit.\n"
"(Holevo's theorem is more general than this.\n"
"Its precise statement is technical and requires explanation, but this is one consequence of it.)\n"
"So, through superdense coding, shared entanglement effectively allows for the *doubling* of the classical information-carrying capacity of sending qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sesuai dengan tema pelajaran ini, salah satu sebab mengapa pengekodan suprapadat menarik ialah ia menunjukkan penggunaan belitan yang konkrit dan (dalam konteks teori maklumat) agak mengagumkan.\n"
"Teorem terkenal dalam teori maklumat kuantum, yang dikenali sebagai *teorem Holevo*, membayangkan bahawa tanpa penggunaan keadaan terikat yang dikongsi, adalah mustahil untuk berkomunikasi lebih daripada satu bit maklumat klasik dengan menghantar satu qubit.\n"
"(Teorem Holevo lebih umum daripada ini.\n"
"Pernyataan tepatnya adalah teknikal dan memerlukan penjelasan, tetapi ini adalah salah satu konsekuensinya.)\n"
"Jadi, melalui pengekodan suprapadat, belitan yang dikongsi secara efektif membolehkan *penggandaan* kapasiti membawa maklumat klasik daripada menghantar qubit.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Protocol {#protocol}"
msgstr "Protokol {#protocol}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following quantum circuit diagram describes the superdense coding protocol:\n"
msgstr "Gambar rajah litar kuantum berikut menerangkan protokol pengekodan suprapadat:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Superdense coding circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/superdense-coding.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Superdense coding circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/superdense-coding.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In words, here is what Alice does:\n"
msgstr "Dalam kata-kata, inilah yang Alice lakukan:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $d=1$, Alice performs a $Z$ gate on her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ (and if $d=0$ she does not).\n"
msgstr "Jika $d=1$, Alice melakukan get $Z$ pada Qubitnya $\\mathsf{A}$ (dan jika $d=0$ dia tidak melakukan apa-apa).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $c=1$, Alice performs an $X$ gate on her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ (and if $c=0$ she does not).\n"
msgstr "Jika $c=1$, Alice melakukan get $X$ pada Qubitnya $\\mathsf{A}$ (dan jika $c=0$ dia tidak melakukan apa-apa).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alice then sends her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ to Bob.\n"
msgstr "Alice kemudian menghantar Qubitnya $\\mathsf{A}$ kepada Bob.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What Bob does when he receives the qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ is to first perform a controlled-NOT gate, with $\\mathsf{A}$ being the control and $\\mathsf{B}$ being the target, and then he applies a Hadamard gate to $\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
"He then measures $\\mathsf{B}$ to obtain $c$ and $\\mathsf{A}$ to obtain $d$, with standard basis measurements in both cases.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apa yang Bob lakukan apabila dia menerima qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ ialah pertama melakukan get NOT-terkawal, dengan $\\mathsf{A}$ sebagai kawalan dan $\\mathsf{B}$ sebagai sasaran, kemudian dia menggunakan get Hadamard pada $\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
"Kemudian dia mengukur $\\mathsf{B}$ untuk mendapatkan $c$ dan $\\mathsf{A}$ untuk mendapatkan $d$, dengan pengukuran asas standard dalam kedua-dua kes.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis {#analysis}"
msgstr "Analisis {#analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The idea behind this protocol is pretty simple:\n"
"Alice effectively chooses which Bell state she would like to be sharing with Bob,\n"
"she sends Bob her qubit, and Bob measures to determine which Bell state Alice chose.\n"
msgstr ""
"Idea di sebalik protokol ini agak mudah:\n"
"Alice secara efektif memilih keadaan Bell mana yang dia ingin kongsi dengan Bob,\n"
"dia menghantar Qubitnya kepada Bob, dan Bob mengukur untuk menentukan keadaan Bell yang Alice pilih.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, they initially share $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$, and depending upon the bits $c$ and $d$, Alice either leaves this state alone or shifts it to one of the other Bell states by applying $\\mathbb{I}$, $X$, $Z$, or $XZ$ to her qubit\n"
"$\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Iaitu, mereka pada awalnya berkongsi $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ dan bergantung pada bit $c$ dan $d,$ Alice sama ada membiarkan keadaan ini atau menukarnya kepada salah satu keadaan Bell yang lain dengan menggunakan $\\mathbb{I},$ $X,$ $Z,$ atau $XZ$ pada Qubitnya\n"
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes XZ) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^-\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes XZ) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^-\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bob's actions have the following effects on the four Bell states:\n"
msgstr "Tindakan Bob mempunyai kesan berikut pada empat keadaan Bell:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 01\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto -\\vert 11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 01\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto -\\vert 11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This can be checked directly, by computing the results of Bob's operations on these states one at a time.\n"
msgstr "Ini boleh diperiksa secara langsung, dengan mengira keputusan operasi Bob pada keadaan-keadaan ini satu persatu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, when Bob performs his measurements, he is able to determine which Bell state Alice chose.\n"
"To verify that the protocol works correctly is a matter of checking each case:\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, apabila Bob melakukan pengukurannya, dia dapat menentukan keadaan Bell yang Alice pilih.\n"
"Untuk mengesahkan bahawa protokol berfungsi dengan betul adalah soal memeriksa setiap kes:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $cd = 00$, then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$. He transforms this state into $\\vert 00\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 00$.\n"
msgstr "Jika $cd = 00$, maka keadaan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ apabila Bob menerima $\\mathsf{A}$ ialah $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$. Dia mengubah keadaan ini kepada $\\vert 00\\rangle$ dan mendapat $cd = 00$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $cd = 01$, then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle$. He transforms this state into $\\vert 01\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 01$.\n"
msgstr "Jika $cd = 01$, maka keadaan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ apabila Bob menerima $\\mathsf{A}$ ialah $\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle$. Dia mengubah keadaan ini kepada $\\vert 01\\rangle$ dan mendapat $cd = 01$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $cd = 10$, then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle$. He transforms this state into $\\vert 10\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 10$.\n"
msgstr "Jika $cd = 10$, maka keadaan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ apabila Bob menerima $\\mathsf{A}$ ialah $\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle$. Dia mengubah keadaan ini kepada $\\vert 10\\rangle$ dan mendapat $cd = 10$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $cd = 11$, then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle$. He transforms this state into $-\\vert 11\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 11$. (The negative-one phase factor has no effect here.)\n"
msgstr "Jika $cd = 11$, maka keadaan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ apabila Bob menerima $\\mathsf{A}$ ialah $\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle$. Dia mengubah keadaan ini kepada $-\\vert 11\\rangle$ dan mendapat $cd = 11$. (Faktor fasa negatif satu tidak memberi kesan di sini.)\n"
